  "why": "Protocol 30 (CAP-84) added SC_ADDRESS_TYPE_MUXED_CONTRACT, written W\u2026: a contract address with a 64-bit routing ID, and host functions that read the ID. Here a contract is called with the W\u2026 form of its own address and returns its ID, 42, so the envelope carries the new ScAddress arm. Readers built on older XDR cannot decode the transaction set at all; readers that decode it must keep the W\u2026 argument and the returned u64 intact.",
